<Project>

  <!--
    Sonar runs on every build.

    The project's rule is zero Sonar issues on changed files, and it used to be enforced by
    remembering to look at the IDE's Problems view. That is a gate only as reliable as the person
    checking it: the first scan run this way found nine issues across six files, several of them
    months old, none of them visible in an otherwise green build.

    As an analyzer package the same rules run inside `dotnet build`, so the gate IS the build and a
    new issue cannot pass unnoticed. The baseline is zero — anything this reports is new.

    PrivateAssets=all: analysis only, nothing ships in the build output.

    This file applies to projects under the repository root, so the assertion harnesses in the
    scratchpad are deliberately unaffected — they are test code held to a different standard.

    To turn it off, delete this file.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="SonarAnalyzer.CSharp" Version="9.32.0.97167">
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
      <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
    </PackageReference>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
